--- verdict ---
  (a) pointwise D'<=S' on [1,6]: yes ; interval-averaged: yes ; provable from (S,D): NO (3rd cumulants)
  (b) D/S=[0.505 0.787 0.848 0.889] (monotone up, <1 on [1,6]); 1-D/S ~ beta^-0.73 (p<1 => no
      crossing in window); structural closure puts D=S at beta=10.7
  (c) Cov(kap,h), Cov(F^2,h) required -> not closed in (S,D); flow identity is single-beta,
      so one run storing h closes them exactly (no hierarchy).
  acid test: free field S=D and every term above vanishes -> comparison is boundary-tight.
